            <ArticleTitle>Canadian Cardiovascular Society guidelines for the diagnosis and management of stable ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>837-49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cjca.2014.05.013</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0828-282X(14)00356-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This overview provides a guideline for the management of stable ischemic heart disease. It represents the work of a primary and secondary panel of participants from across Canada who achieved consensus on behalf of the Canadian Cardiovascular Society. The suggestions and recommendations are intended to be of relevance to primary care and specialist physicians with an emphasis on rational deployment of diagnostic tests, expedited implementation of long- and short-term medical therapy, timely consideration of revascularization, and practical follow-up measures.</AbstractText>
